.TH FZF-REVAMPED 1 "2026-11-16" "fzf-revamped" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fzf-revamped \- switch, kill, rename or create sessions, windows and panes in fzf
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fzf-revamped
.RI [ options ]
.B apply
.br
.B fzf-revamped
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.B list
.br
.B fzf-revamped
.BR session | window | pane
.RB [ switch | kill ]
.br
.B fzf-revamped
.BR tree | create | palette | cheatsheet | zoxide | last
.br
.B fzf-revamped urls
.RB [ open | copy ]
.br
.B fzf-revamped process
.RI [ signal ]
.br
.B fzf-revamped rename
.RB [ session | window ]
.br
.B fzf-revamped multi\-kill
.RB [ session | window | pane ]
.br
.B fzf-revamped broadcast
.RI [ text ]
.br
.B fzf-revamped move\-window
.RB [ move | link ]
.br
.B fzf-revamped preview
.I target
.br
.B fzf-revamped doctor
.br
.B fzf-revamped version
.br
.B fzf-revamped help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fzf-revamped
lists tmux sessions, windows, panes, URLs, commands, key bindings, processes
or zoxide folders in fzf and acts on the one picked. The entry point
.B fzf-revamped.tmux
runs
.B apply
once when tmux loads the plugin, and every binding goes to tmux in one call;
when one key is invalid, the others are still bound. Each key opens a popup,
or a window before tmux 3.2, that runs one of the commands below.
.PP
Every list line carries its target as a hidden first column, so a name with a
space or a slash still resolves. Run with no command on a terminal, it offers a
menu.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B apply
Bind the keys now.
.TP
.B list
Print every binding apply would make, one per line.
.TP
.BR session | window | pane " [" switch | kill ]
Switch the client to the one picked, or kill it.
.TP
.B tree
Pick any session, window or pane and go there.
.TP
.B create
Switch to the session picked, or create one named after what was typed.
.TP
.BR urls " [" open | copy ]
Open a URL on the screen with xdg-open or open, or copy it into a tmux buffer.
.TP
.B palette
Run a tmux command from a short list.
.TP
.B cheatsheet
Browse every key binding.
.TP
.BI process " [signal]"
Send a signal, TERM by default, to the process picked, after a yes.
.TP
.BR rename " [" session | window ]
Rename the one picked to the name typed at a prompt in the popup.
An empty answer renames nothing.
.TP
.BR multi\-kill " [" session | window | pane ]
Kill every one marked, after a yes.
.TP
.BI broadcast " [text]"
Type the text and Enter into every pane marked. Without text, it reads and
clears
.BR @fzf_revamped_broadcast_text ,
which the broadcast key's prompt fills.
.TP
.B zoxide
Open a session at a zoxide folder.
.TP
.B last
Switch to the last session.
.TP
.BR move\-window " [" move | link ]
Move or link the window picked to a session typed at a prompt in the
popup. An empty answer moves nothing.
.TP
.BI preview " target"
Print a pane, for the switch preview.
.TP
.B doctor
Print one row per dependency: tmux, fzf, the opener, zoxide, gum, a default key
someone else holds, and the core tools. Exits 1 only when a required tool is
missing.
.TP
.B version
Print the version, then the tmux version.
.TP
.B help
Print the help page.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
.B list
prints one JSON object.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " name"
Colours of the terminal interface:
.BR kodougu ,
.BR catppuccin\-mocha ,
.BR catppuccin\-latte ,
.BR dracula ,
.BR nord ,
.BR gruvbox ,
.B tokyo\-night
or
.BR mono .
The default is
.BR kodougu .
.TP
.BI \-\- setting " value"
Any tmux option below, named with dashes, such as
.B \-\-session\-key
or
.BR \-\-mru .
It also takes the form
.IR \-\-setting = value .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FZF_REVAMPED_SETTING
Any tmux option below in capitals, such as
.BR FZF_REVAMPED_MRU .
The command line wins over the environment, and the environment over the
tmux option.
.TP
.B FZF_REVAMPED_THEME
The theme when
.B \-\-theme
is not given.
.TP
.B FZF_REVAMPED_ACCENT
A colour such as #CBA6F7 that replaces the accent of the theme.
.TP
.B KODOUGU_THEME
The theme of every kodougu and tmux-revamped tool, when neither
.B \-\-theme
nor
.B FZF_REVAMPED_THEME
is set.
.TP
.B KODOUGU_ACCENT
The accent of every kodougu and tmux-revamped tool, when
.B FZF_REVAMPED_ACCENT
is not set.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Turns colour off in every theme.
.SH TMUX OPTIONS
An empty tmux option means its default, and a key set to
.B off
binds nothing.
.TP
.B @fzf_revamped_palette_key
The palette. The default is
.BR M-f ;
a key someone else already bound is left alone and
.B doctor
reports it.
.TP
.BR @fzf_revamped_session_key ", " @fzf_revamped_window_key ", " @fzf_revamped_pane_key
The session, window and pane switchers. Unbound by default.
.TP
.BR @fzf_revamped_kill_key ", " @fzf_revamped_multikill_key
The session killer and the session multi-kill. Unbound by default.
.TP
.BR @fzf_revamped_tree_key ", " @fzf_revamped_create_key ", " @fzf_revamped_url_key ", " @fzf_revamped_cheatsheet_key
The tree, create or switch, the URL opener and the cheatsheet. Unbound by
default.
.TP
.BR @fzf_revamped_process_key ", " @fzf_revamped_rename_key ", " @fzf_revamped_broadcast_key
The process signaller, the window renamer and the broadcast prompt. Unbound by
default.
.TP
.BR @fzf_revamped_zoxide_key ", " @fzf_revamped_last_key ", " @fzf_revamped_move_key
The zoxide sessions, the last session and the window mover. Unbound by
default.
.TP
.BR @fzf_revamped_popup_width ", " @fzf_revamped_popup_height
The popup size. The defaults are
.B 60%
and
.BR 50% .
.TP
.B @fzf_revamped_popup_border
The popup border on tmux 3.4 and later:
.BR rounded ,
.BR single ,
.BR double ,
.BR heavy ,
.BR simple ,
.B padded
or
.BR none .
The default is
.BR rounded .
.TP
.B @fzf_revamped_preview
.B on
or
.B 1
shows the pane under the cursor in the switch pickers.
.TP
.B @fzf_revamped_mru
.B on
orders the sessions by their last attach.
.TP
.B @revamped_theme
The theme of every tmux-revamped tool, when nothing else sets one. The default
is
.BR kodougu .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on any failure, an invalid key included.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tmux (1),
.BR fzf (1),
.BR zoxide (1),
.BR gum (1)
